  "instance_name": "iq_score_context",
  "label": "IQ Score Context",
  "description": "The meme references the concept of IQ (Intelligence Quotient) as a standardized measure of cognitive ability. An IQ score of 80 is generally considered below average (average is 100), and the meme's humor stems from the contrast between this score and the implied social status of being the 'highest in your village.' This requires background knowledge about IQ scoring systems and their interpretation in different cultural and educational contexts.",
